          <baseCommit>bc34b0f8ab8cfd0bc44ef6ce3b964a07f0a32c18</baseCommit>
          <output>**A04_01_CopyData executed.** Summary:

- Copied the full `a03_authoring/data` tree (1 DocSet, 34 pages, 9 page groups) into `a04_rendering/data`, remapping package `a03_authoring.data` → `a04_rendering.data`, prefixes `a03pgroup`/`a03data` → `a04pgroup`/`a04data`, and `BmlDocSet_A03` → `BmlDocSet_A04` (file renamed too).
- Updated self-identifying sector prose (&quot;A03 page group&quot;, &quot;A03 documentation set&quot;, etc.) to A04, while leaving historical provenance text (&quot;Body content is authored in a03/A03 …&quot;) untouched since that's still factually true and matches the precedent from the prior A02→A03 copy.
- Rewrote the DocSet's pipeline-provenance sentence to describe A04's actual process (copied by `A04_01_CopyData`, then rendered by `A04_02_RenderPages`) instead of a blind numeric substitution that would have wrongly referenced a nonexistent `A04_02_AuthorPages`.
- Left `a04_rendering/task` and `A04_RenderingSector` untouched; made no changes to A03 or any other sector.
- Added new `xmlns` prefixes (`a04data`, `a04docs`, `a04pgroup`) and catalogued every imported A04 Block in `Library.bml`.
- Ran `npx blockml validate --all`: no new errors; the only errors present are 5 pre-existing ones in frozen historical `_meta/transform/succeeded` records, unrelated to this change.
- `inspect`ed `BmlDocSet_A04` — fully resolved, zero unresolved references, pages/pageGroups/homePage/rootPageGroup all point at A04 Blocks.

I did not commit — the working tree changes are `Library.bml` (modified) and the new `a04_rendering/data/` tree, ready for the transform tool to commit as `transform(operation)`.</output>
